[{"model":"Logistic regression","kind":"predictive","steps":[{"step":"impute","class":"SimpleImputer","params":{"add_indicator":false,"copy":true,"keep_empty_features":false,"missing_values":null,"strategy":"median"}},{"step":"scale","class":"StandardScaler","params":{"copy":true,"with_mean":true,"with_std":true}},{"step":"clf","class":"LogisticRegression","params":{"C":0.3,"dual":false,"fit_intercept":true,"intercept_scaling":1,"l1_ratio":0.0,"max_iter":5000,"penalty":"deprecated","solver":"lbfgs","tol":0.0001,"warm_start":false}}],"why":"The interpretable reference. Strong L2 regularisation, because 83 features against roughly 1,100 training rows will otherwise overfit. Its standardised coefficients are what the driver chart reports, and on the harder task it is the best of the four.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.8976,"lo":0.8556,"hi":0.9331,"pr_auc":0.8438,"precision_at_30":0.9667,"brier":0.1876},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.6052,"lo":0.505,"hi":0.6989,"pr_auc":0.2222,"precision_at_30":0.3,"brier":0.1816}}},{"model":"Gradient boosting","kind":"predictive","steps":[{"step":"clf","class":"HistGradientBoostingClassifier","params":{"categorical_features":"from_dtype","early_stopping":"auto","l2_regularization":1.0,"learning_rate":0.06,"loss":"log_loss","max_bins":255,"max_depth":3,"max_features":1.0,"max_iter":300,"max_leaf_nodes":31,"min_samples_leaf":15,"n_iter_no_change":10,"scoring":"loss","tol":0.0,"validation_fraction":0.1,"warm_start":false}}],"why":"Deliberately shallow: depth 3, and at least 15 samples per leaf. Chosen partly because it handles missing values natively, and 14% of the design matrix is missing in a way that is informative rather than random.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.9294,"lo":0.8973,"hi":0.9566,"pr_auc":0.8727,"precision_at_30":0.9667,"brier":0.104},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.5344,"lo":0.4187,"hi":0.6469,"pr_auc":0.2239,"precision_at_30":0.3333,"brier":0.159}}},{"model":"Gradient boosting (calibrated)","kind":"predictive","steps":[{"step":"clf","class":"CalibratedClassifierCV","params":{"cv":3,"ensemble":"auto","method":"isotonic"}}],"why":"The same model with isotonic calibration. Whoever acts on a triage score reads it as a probability, so it has to be one. This moves the Brier score on the level task from 0.19 to 0.089 while barely changing the ranking.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.9465,"lo":0.9194,"hi":0.9689,"pr_auc":0.9039,"precision_at_30":0.9667,"brier":0.0886},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.5522,"lo":0.4388,"hi":0.6614,"pr_auc":0.2449,"precision_at_30":0.3,"brier":0.1562}}},{"model":"Neural network (MC dropout)","kind":"predictive","steps":[{"step":"impute","class":"SimpleImputer","params":{"add_indicator":false,"copy":true,"keep_empty_features":false,"missing_values":null,"strategy":"median"}},{"step":"scale","class":"StandardScaler","params":{"copy":true,"with_mean":true,"with_std":true}},{"step":"clf","class":"MCDropoutMLP","params":{"batch_size":128,"dropout":0.3,"hidden":[64,32],"lr":0.003,"max_epochs":400,"mc_samples":100,"patience":40,"val_fraction":0.2,"weight_decay":0.001}}],"why":"Not expected to win on this sample size, and it does not. It is here for the uncertainty: dropout left switched on at inference gives an approximate posterior, so each authority carries a spread rather than a point estimate. Early stopping on a held-out slice of the training years, and a reweighted loss for the small positive class.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.9279,"lo":0.8926,"hi":0.9564,"pr_auc":0.8858,"precision_at_30":0.9667,"brier":0.1854},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.5853,"lo":0.4857,"hi":0.6818,"pr_auc":0.2242,"precision_at_30":0.2667,"brier":0.1661}}},{"model":"Persistence baseline","kind":"baseline","steps":[],"why":"Not a fitted model. Last year's value for the level task, last year's change for escalation. This is what a service already has without any analytics, and two of the three findings come from it.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.9004,"lo":0.8431,"hi":0.948,"pr_auc":0.8843,"precision_at_30":0.9667,"brier":null},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.3454,"lo":0.2583,"hi":0.436,"pr_auc":0.1146,"precision_at_30":0.0333,"brier":null}}},{"model":"Prevalence (no model)","kind":"baseline","steps":[],"why":"Predicts the base rate for everyone. It fixes the floor, so that a hit rate in a fixed-length list has a meaning to compare against.","results":{"Level":{"roc_auc":0.5,"lo":null,"hi":null,"pr_auc":0.3213,"precision_at_30":0.3213,"brier":0.2277},"Escalation":{"roc_auc":0.5,"lo":null,"hi":null,"pr_auc":0.1489,"precision_at_30":0.1489,"brier":0.1548}}}]